    <item>
      <title>US Labor Market Is Failing to Provide Quality Jobs for Workers</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-10-05/us-labor-market-is-failing-to-provide-quality-jobs-for-workers</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">c061b666762760101250f535</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 10:00:03 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>A US government report Friday showed that the unemployment rate ticked higher to 4.2% in September from 4.1% in August. That’s still pretty low by historical standards. But the stability seems illusory, given we seem to be stuck in a labor market that rather than adding high-paying jobs, is dominated by lower-earning positions. No wonder purchasing power is slipping and workers are dissatisfied.</description>
